WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.560
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:11.600
Today we are going to talk about OpenAI’s&nbsp;
amazing image generator AI, DALL-E 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:17.680
and you will see that it can do two things&nbsp;
that perhaps not many of you have heard of.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:26.240
So, what is DALL-E 2? This is a diffusion-based AI&nbsp;
model, which means that it starts out from noise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:33.920
and gradually changes it to become a beautiful&nbsp;
image like this one. The image can be anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:41.040
so much so that we can enter a piece of text,&nbsp;
and magically, out comes an image that fits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:47.680
this description. It would be hard to overstate&nbsp;
how transformative this will be to digital art.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:54.720
Imagine that you could now illustrate any&nbsp;
novel…and not only that, but it wouldn’t even need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.080
any additional work for you&nbsp;
to write up the text prompts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:04.480
Just take excerpts from the&nbsp;
novel, and there we go. Wow.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:12.080
And, if you feel like adding crazy prompts, as&nbsp;
you see, it won’t complain about that either. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.360
it can do even more. For instance, if&nbsp;
we have an image that we really like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:24.640
variant generation is also possible. This means&nbsp;
that we can provide it an input image, it tries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:32.320
to understand what it depicts, and create several&nbsp;
versions of it. And it does that spectacularly.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:40.080
But, that’s not the only little-known&nbsp;
feature is does, it also two other amazing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:48.720
things. One is image inpainting. What is that?
Inpainting means that we take an input image&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:56.240
or video, cut out an undesirable part, and let&nbsp;
an algorithm fill in the holes with data that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:04.000
makes sense given the context of this image. Now,&nbsp;
previous techniques were already capable of this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:11.600
but I am very excited to see what DALL-E 2 can do&nbsp;
with this problem, because we know that it has a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:18.240
really detailed understanding of the world around&nbsp;
us. So, can it use its knowledge of the world to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:25.200
create high-quality inpaintings? Oh boy, you will&nbsp;
see in a moment that it can do it incredibly well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:33.600
Let’s give it a try. Oh yes, we can delete this&nbsp;
squirrel, and here comes the key: oh my! Remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:40.080
that I said that inpainting techniques fill&nbsp;
in the holes given the context of the image.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:47.600
But DALL-E 2 does something even better! It fills&nbsp;
in the image with any context we can think of.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:54.880
Let’s try that! How? Well, this image is&nbsp;
ridiculous - squirrels are known not to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:03:04.800
able to operate computers, so, let’s add a hippo&nbsp;
instead. And there we go! Much better. Loving it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.520
Now let’s push it to the limits&nbsp;
through 5 outstanding examples!

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:16.240
One. The ladybug. Here is a&nbsp;
photo, but, look. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:23.600
some parts of the photo are out of focus. Oh&nbsp;
yes, how about deleting those parts, and have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:31.840
them inpainted with DALL-E 2? Could that work? It&nbsp;
knows that this is a ladybug after all. Let’s see.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:39.920
Wow. That is much sharper and fits the&nbsp;
image really well. I would have to look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:46.400
for quite a bit to find out the trickery. What&nbsp;
about you? Let me know in the comments below! So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:53.840
this is fantastic. But you know what is even&nbsp;
more fantastic? Now hold on to your papers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.840 --> 00:04:00.480
because it can also do not only image&nbsp;
inpainting, but image outpainting!

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:10.240
What is that? Well, two. Ever wondered what might&nbsp;
be outside of this frame? Well, let’s ask DALL-E&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:20.160
2 and…that is insanity. It is really doing it. And&nbsp;
we can just zoom out and out and out and it feels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:26.880
like it never stops. And it just gets crazier&nbsp;
over time. If a human would have made this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:34.080
I would say that human is very creative. But&nbsp;
this was done by a machine. Is that a hint of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:42.480
creativity in a machine? Food for thought.&nbsp;
I love this one. What a time to be alive!

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:50.320
Three, of course, we need to do that to the&nbsp;
Mona Lisa too. What could be outside the frame?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:58.640
Ah, I see! This is a more modern take on&nbsp;
the old classic. Working at the office while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:04.480
everyone else is enjoying life. Note that&nbsp;
once again, a prompt was used to generate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:10.080
the theme of the outpainting here. These are&nbsp;
the prompts that were used for this example.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:16.480
And, these are so good, let’s do a&nbsp;
couple more. Four. Zooming out from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:23.040
a house in the middle of a lush field to&nbsp;
this. Very artistic. And it turns out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:30.160
wow…that we are on a floating island in&nbsp;
the middle of the universe…with a twist.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:40.080
And, last, but not least. Five, the Last Supper.&nbsp;
But this time, let’s not zoom out, but let’s try&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:47.760
to answer one of history’s big questions: and that&nbsp;
is, what might be going on in the adjacent rooms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:57.280
Look. I love it. And I wonder what DALL-E&nbsp;
3 will be capable of? Remember, the DALL-E&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:04.160
2 version came out just about a year after the&nbsp;
first version, and it was leaps and bounds better.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:11.360
And the competition is also coming, Google&nbsp;
already has their Imagen and Parti AI’s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:17.920
and even that is just scratching the surface. As&nbsp;
you see, the pace of progress in AI research is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:24.000
absolutely incredible. These tools are going&nbsp;
to transform the world around us as we know it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:32.640
especially now that OpenAI is aiming to deploy&nbsp;
this AI to no less than 1 million people in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:40.880
near future. How cool is that! Democratizing&nbsp;
art creation for all of us. Soon. Bravo!

